# ---------------------------------
#   KD's Homebrew Linux Distro
# ---------------------------------

KK is a fork of BB, the AAlib demo.

    BB — the portable demo
    Copyright (C) 1997 AA-group
        Filip Kupsa (FK), Mojmir Svoboda (MS),
        Kamil Toman (KT), Jan Hubicka (HH)
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
    See COPYING and AUTHORS, both carried unchanged.

KK is distributed under the same terms. The fractal engine is still XaoS's,
the timer library, the renderer glue, the text formatter, the LZO image
format and most of the scenes are still AA-group's work, and the demo's
credits scene says so on screen.

This file records what KDOS changed, so nobody has to diff a 1997 tarball to
find out.


## Removed

* **The autotools layer.** configure, configure.in, Makefile.am/.in,
  aclocal.m4, acconfig.h, aconfig.h.in, install-sh, missing, mkinstalldirs,
  stamp-h. KK targets one platform — KDOS: musl, Linux, x86_64 — so
  src/aconfig.h is written down rather than probed, and the port's build.sh
  compiles the tree directly.

* **The DOS, OS/2, Windows, Amiga and Plan 9 paths.** ctrl87.c/.h were an
  8087 control-word setter in i386 assembly whose body compiled to nothing on
  x86_64; the four `_control87()` calls in zoom.c went with them. config.h's
  `#ifdef __DJGPP__ #include "aconfig.dos"` and scene7.c's `#ifdef _plan9_`
  block are gone.

* **The four AA-group portraits** — fk[1-4].c, hh[1-4].c, kt[1-4].c,
  ms[1-4].c, about a megabyte of LZO-compressed photographs, and the four
  1997 biographies in bb.c. KK carries one portrait instead. Their names and
  their work stay in the credits scene, in AUTHORS and here; the GPL asks for
  the copyright notices, not for the photographs.

* **The three original modules** bb.s3m, bb2.s3m, bb3.s3m (1.3 MB), replaced
  by three public-domain tracks — see music/MUSIC.credits.

* **The interactive startup.** Upstream's main() asked "Music?[Y/n]" and then
  offered a keyboard-driven mixer menu — 16-bit, stereo, sample rate — before
  drawing anything. A demo that ships as a system command has to start when
  it is started: the settings are compiled in and `--no-sound` covers the one
  question that mattered.


## Fixed

Both of these are real defects that reached KDOS, found with AddressSanitizer
rather than by reading:

* **tex.c `clear_zbuff()` cleared twice its allocation.** `set_zbuff()`
  allocates `X_s * Y_s * sizeof(int)` and the clear used `sizeof(long)` —
  identical on the 32-bit machines this was written for, double on x86_64.
  It corrupts the heap and aborts stage 2 with "malloc(): corrupted top size".

* **messager.c `newline()` scrolled the text buffer with `memcpy`.** Source
  and destination overlap by every row but one. That is undefined behaviour;
  glibc happened to survive it, and musl is free not to.


## Added

* `src/kk.c`, `src/kk.h` — options, the frame counter, `--fps`,
  `--benchmark`, `--scene`, `--driver`.
* `src/kdos_intro.c` — the CRT power-on and the KDOS wordmark.
* `src/kdos_penguin.c` — the mascot, decoded from
  `src/packages/kdos-splash/penguin.h`, which is INCLUDED rather than copied:
  the boot splash, the login banner and this demo must not be able to end up
  wearing different birds.
* `src/fx_matrix.c`, `src/fx_tunnel.c`, `src/fx_rotozoom.c`,
  `src/fx_scope.c` — new scenes. The scope is the one that listens: bar
  heights from `Voice_RealVolume()`, beats from `Player_GetRow()`.
* `src/kd[1-4].c` — the portrait, GENERATED by `tools/genface.c` from
  `face/face.txt`. Same `struct image` format as the originals.
* `face/face.txt` — the baked greyscale portrait, lifted from the FACE table
  in generate_profile.py of https://github.com/kunaldawn/kunaldawn.
* `music/` — three public-domain modules and their provenance.


## Changed

* `src/main.c` registers every MikMod loader, not just S3M.
* `SOUNDDIR` is `/usr/share/kk`, and the modules are installed there
  unconditionally. Upstream's `pkgdata_DATA` only installed them when
  libmikmod was found at configure time, which is how a mute binary ships.
* The scene script in `bb.c` and the credits text are KDOS's.
